Hello guys! Want to share my thoughts regarding the minting process overall- maybe something would be useful. 

For now minting is divided between Cornucopias community as follows: 
1.OG that get's the digital asset with the most probability;
2. Holders that minted/purchased digital assets previously;
3. Cornucopians that are registered on server for at least 1 month.

The first  OG role was given for early server participants and afterwards to people that are helpful. But the problem is that that many OG on this server don't have any assets (didn't mint or selled them), which could mean that they are passive and not interested in the ecosystem. My suggestion is that their OG roles should be passed for later ones Cornucopian that are long term asset holders. Another one suggestion is that OG role should be defragmented, for example, Tier 1 Early OG and Tier 2 long term holder etc., - that would highlight and give privileges to long term asset holders that are more interested in the Cornucopias.

